<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Ceiba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Ceiba is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> coast of northern Honduras and capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of Atlántida. It grew from the late nineteenth century as the base of the Vaccaro brothers' banana business, later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/standard-fruit-company">Standard Fruit Company</a>, whose railways and docks made it one of the country's main export ports. It is one of the largest cities in Honduras and a gateway to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-islands">Bay Islands</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-ceiba.jpg" alt="La Ceiba" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: InterCoined · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Letras_de_La_Ceiba.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
